# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this Astro project by following the latest official documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 1.4.1) using npm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the resolved dependency tree

### 2. Analytics Integration
Modified `src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro`:
- Added import statement: `import { inject } from '@vercel/analytics';`
- Called `inject()` function in the component script section to initialize analytics tracking

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation for Astro projects, I used the `inject()` function approach which:
- Automatically tracks page views across all pages using the base layout
- Initializes the analytics script on every page render
- Works seamlessly with Astro's static site generation

The analytics component is now active on all pages that use the BaseLayout (which includes all main pages of the site).

## Verification

1. ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
2. ✅ All 107 tests passed without issues
3. ✅ No linting errors introduced
4. ✅ Lock file properly updated

## Next Steps for Activation

To fully enable Web Analytics on Vercel:
1. Deploy this change to your Vercel project
2. Navigate to the Analytics tab in your Vercel dashboard
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate tracking
4. Verify analytics are working by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

## Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency resolution
- `src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro` - Added analytics initialization
